  "body": "This came up in #4350. The problem is that these members assume there's always a browsing context. But really, once it's been (synchronously) discarded, it's gone, so there needs to be some kind of null check on a `Window` object's pointer to one.\r\n\r\n(This is probably a somewhat wider problem, but fixing it in pieces seems okay. If adventurous one might also want to investigate which of `Window`/settings objects/`Document`/Realm/agent would be the logical place to hold the actual pointer.)",
